With {nu}, {na'e bo lo nu ...} is a problem, because there's a huge class
of almost exactly identical events for any given "event". This is the same
problem as having an outer quantifier on an event. The {lo na'e nu ...}
solution is better here.

mu'o mi'e la latro'a

